  "notes": [
    "The ten entries the sheet's race picker offers, before the bestiary starts at column L (bat). The other 970-odd creature columns are Concept 04's bestiary — a later milestone, not a race list.",
    "The sheet stores an **absolute base** per stat; the v1 Race shape stores modifiers. They agree only because a stat's default base is 0, so \"modifier 10\" and \"base 10\" are the same number today. TICKET-RACE-01 makes them bases properly, and TICKET-RACE-02 adds the blend — until then, picking two races adds their blocks instead of averaging them.",
    "Totals in each description are the sheet's own row 14 and are the six-core-only check Concept 01 confirms: human 60, elf 64, dwarf 60, Raccoon 59, Demon 90.",
    "\"Empty\" is the sheet's no-race placeholder — all zeros — and is kept because the race picker offers it."
